---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SocialLinks from '../components/SocialLinks.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Cian O'Leary - AI Infrastructure Engineer">
  <Header />
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">About</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg">
      <p class="text-text-secondary">
        I'm an AI Infrastructure Engineer focused on building systems that scale. My work sits at the intersection of distributed systems, machine learning operations, and developer tooling — the critical foundation that enables AI products to perform reliably in production.
      </p>

      <p class="text-text-secondary">
        With a background in software engineering and a growing interest in the infrastructure layer of AI systems, I'm working toward positioning myself in the AI infrastructure space. I write about what I'm learning, building, and thinking about in this rapidly evolving field.
      </p>

      <p class="text-text-secondary">
        When I'm not building, you'll find me writing about systems design, exploring new tools and frameworks, and thinking about how to make AI infrastructure more accessible and robust.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-border my-12" />

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">What I Believe</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-text-secondary">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-text-primary">Infrastructure is foundational.</strong> The best ML models are worthless without the systems to deploy, scale, and maintain them. I'm focused on the unsexy but critical work that makes AI products actually work.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-text-primary">Simplicity over cleverness.</strong> Distributed systems are complex enough without adding unnecessary layers. I prefer clear, maintainable solutions over clever ones that nobody else can understand.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-text-primary">Documentation matters.</strong> Infrastructure that's not documented doesn't exist. The real test of understanding is whether you can explain it clearly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="border-border my-12" />

    <section class="text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Connect</h2>
      <SocialLinks />
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>